</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4. </span>Cache Configurator</h3>

<section id="S3.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.4.1. </span>Problem Formulation</h4>

<div id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider a MoE model <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers, each with <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> experts, where only <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ll N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≪</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ll N</annotation></semantics></math>) experts are sparsely activated per token.
Given the target device <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, we denote its PCIe bandwidth and VRAM capacity as <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Let <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> be the total model size, with <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> indicating the size of all non-expert parameters.
Hence, the size of each expert can be expressed as <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{e}=\frac{U-U_{n}}{LN}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{e}=\frac{U-U_{n}}{LN}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the time for loading an expert is given by <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{load}^{e}=U_{e}/B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{load}^{e}=U_{e}/B</annotation></semantics></math>.
We can profile each module’s execution time of model <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}</annotation></semantics></math> over device <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, including that of attention module <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{comp}^{att}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{comp}^{att}</annotation></semantics></math>, MoE module <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{comp}^{moe}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{comp}^{moe}</annotation></semantics></math>, and head layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{comp}^{head}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{comp}^{head}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We omit the computation time of router network, as it constitutes a negligible fraction of the overall inference latency.
Besides, <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the available time window for prefetching experts in layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the first layer, the prefetching window involves the time for processing the previous token in the head layer and the time for the attention module in the first layer, <span id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{1}=T_{comp}^{head}+T_{comp}^{att}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{1}=T_{comp}^{head}+T_{comp}^{att}</annotation></semantics></math>.
During each prefetching window <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">MoEpic</span> proactively prefetches experts for layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> by descending order of their predicted scores.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the allocated VRAM budget and the cache size (<span id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, number of cached experts) in layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
The expert split ratio is then computed as <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}=V_{i}/C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}=V_{i}/C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given the cache size <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and prefetching window <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of each layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we assume that after the process of layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s router network, <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> activated experts are fully loaded into VRAM, <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> activated experts have only their top segments cached in VRAM, and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> activated experts remain completely offloaded in RAM.
The values of <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are critically dependent on both the cache hit rate and the expert prediction accuracy of layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
As previously introduced, once obtaining the routing result, <span id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">MoEpic</span> starts to process the already-loaded activated experts while simultaneously fetching the missed experts.
Let <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{comp}^{exp}=T_{comp}^{moe}/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{comp}^{exp}=T_{comp}^{moe}/K</annotation></semantics></math> represents the time for processing one expert.
Consequently, we can formulate the expert computation time for hiding the missed expert loading latency as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{hide}^{i}=(\alpha_{i}+\beta_{i}\theta_{i})\cdot T_{comp}^{exp},\quad i\in[L]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{hide}^{i}=(\alpha_{i}+\beta_{i}\theta_{i})\cdot T_{comp}^{exp},\quad i\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the latency for fetching an expert from RAM to VRAM as <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{load}^{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{load}^{exp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the latency for loading the missed experts and/or segments in layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{miss}^{i}=[\beta_{i}(1-\theta_{i})+\gamma_{i}]\cdot T_{load}^{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{miss}^{i}=[\beta_{i}(1-\theta_{i})+\gamma_{i}]\cdot T_{load}^{exp}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, the expert loading latency that can not be overlapped by the GPU computation is formulated as:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{i}=\max\{0,T_{miss}^{i}-T_{hide}^{i}\},\quad i\in[L]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{i}=\max\{0,T_{miss}^{i}-T_{hide}^{i}\},\quad i\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">At this point, we can derive the expected value of each layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s prefetching window <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{i}=(T_{comp}^{moe}-\min\{T_{hide}^{i-1},T_{miss}^{i-1}\})+T_{comp}^{att},\quad 2\leq i\leq L" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{i}=(T_{comp}^{moe}-\min\{T_{hide}^{i-1},T_{miss}^{i-1}\})+T_{comp}^{att},\quad 2\leq i\leq L</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To improve the response speed of the MoE inference with expert offloading, the optimization problem in <span id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">MoEpic</span> aims to minimize the non-overlapped expert loading latency by determining the optimal VRAM budgets and expert split ratios across different layers:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{V_{i},\theta_{i}(i\in[L])}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathcal{T}^{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{V_{i},\theta_{i}(i\in[L])}\sum_{i=1}^{L}\mathcal{T}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s.t.\begin{cases}U_{n}+\sum_{i=1}^{L}V_{i}+U_{b}\leq V&amp;\\
\alpha_{i}+\beta_{i}+\gamma_{i}=K,&amp;\forall i\in[L]\\
V_{i}&gt;0,\theta_{i}\in(0,1],&amp;\forall i\in[L]\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s.t.\begin{cases}U_{n}+\sum_{i=1}^{L}V_{i}+U_{b}\leq V&amp;\\
\alpha_{i}+\beta_{i}+\gamma_{i}=K,&amp;\forall i\in[L]\\
V_{i}&gt;0,\theta_{i}\in(0,1],&amp;\forall i\in[L]\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where the first inequality meets the VRAM constraint, and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the buffer size.
The second set of inequalities indicates that the activated experts in each layer can only be in three statuses: fully loaded, only the top segment loaded, or completely unloaded.
The third sets of inequalities specify the feasible ranges for the optimization variables <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS4.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>), respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.4.2. </span>Algorithm Design</h4>

<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">However, since obtaining the precise values of <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is quite difficult in practice, it is infeasible to directly solve this optimization problem.
To tackle this issue, we design a divide-and-conquer algorithm based on fixed-point iteration to optimize the cache configuration of <span id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">MoEpic</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To begin with, we decompose the complex and intractable optimization problem in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.4.1. Problem Formulation ‣ 3.4. Cache Configurator ‣ 3. System Design ‣ Accelerating Mixture-of-Expert Inference with Adaptive Expert Split Mechanism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) and focus on a more manageable sub-problem.
Specifically, given the VRAM budget <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and the prefetching window <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for a specific layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we aim to determine the optimal expert split ratio <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the exposed loading latency <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
To solve this sub-problem, <span id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif">MoEpic</span> records the (predicted) experts scores for each token at every layer, and derives the following three probabilities for layer <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> after the inference of <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> tokens:</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cache Hit Rate <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{i}(C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{i}(C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the number of times the activated experts hit the cache with a cache size of <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>), divided by the total number of activated experts (<span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\cdot K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\cdot K</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Expert Prediction Accuracy <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{i}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{i}(y)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the activation frequency of the expert with <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>-th highest predicted score (<math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>), divided by the total number of processed tokens (<span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prediction Cache Hit Rate <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{PH}_{i}(y,C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏𝐇</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{PH}_{i}(y,C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the number of times the expert with <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>-th highest predicted score hits the cache with a cache size of <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, divided by the total number of processed tokens.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we relax the discrete count of activated experts into a continuous optimization variable.
Concretely, we assume that after the prefetch operation with window size <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in[0,K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in[0,K]</annotation></semantics></math>) activated experts are already loaded in VRAM.
At this point, the goal of minimizing exposed loading latency <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to maximizing <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a cache size of <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the amount of cached activated experts is <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{cache}^{i}(\theta_{i},C_{i})=K\cdot\mathbf{H}_{i}(C_{i})\cdot\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{cache}^{i}(\theta_{i},C_{i})=K\cdot\mathbf{H}_{i}(C_{i})\cdot\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, considering the prefetch operation for the <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>-th predicted expert (<span id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, expert with <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>-th highest predicted score), its expected execution time <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{pref}^{i}(a,C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{pref}^{i}(a,C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})=[1-\mathbf{PH_{i}}(y,C_{i})\cdot\theta_{i}]\cdot T_{load}^{exp}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏𝐇</mi><mi>𝐢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})=[1-\mathbf{PH_{i}}(y,C_{i})\cdot\theta_{i}]\cdot T_{load}^{exp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, we can quantify the expected loading amount of activated experts <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> under this prefetch operation:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})=[1-\mathbf{PH_{i}}(y,C_{i})\cdot\theta_{i}]\cdot\mathbf{P}_{i}(y,C_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏𝐇</mi><mi>𝐢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})=[1-\mathbf{PH_{i}}(y,C_{i})\cdot\theta_{i}]\cdot\mathbf{P}_{i}(y,C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that at most <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> expert prefetch operations can be completed within the window <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{wind}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{wind}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, the formulation for the sub-problem optimization is given as the following Eq. (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.4.2. Algorithm Design ‣ 3.4. Cache Configurator ‣ 3. System Design ‣ Accelerating Mixture-of-Expert Inference with Adaptive Expert Split Mechanism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), which can be easily solved by searching the optimal cache size <math id="S3.SS4.SSS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{C_{i}\in[N]}m_{i}=A_{cache}^{i}(\theta_{i},C_{i})+\sum_{y=1}^{Y}A_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Y</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{C_{i}\in[N]}m_{i}=A_{cache}^{i}(\theta_{i},C_{i})+\sum_{y=1}^{Y}A_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(11)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s.t.\begin{cases}\theta_{i}=V_{i}/C_{i}\\
\sum_{y=1}^{Y}T_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})\leq T_{wind}^{i}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>Y</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s.t.\begin{cases}\theta_{i}=V_{i}/C_{i}\\
\sum_{y=1}^{Y}T_{pref}^{i}(y,C_{i})\leq T_{wind}^{i}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Cache Configuration Algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="alg1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Latency metrics <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{comp}^{att}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{comp}^{att}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{comp}^{moe}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{comp}^{moe}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{comp}^{head}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{comp}^{head}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{load}^{exp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{load}^{exp}</annotation></semantics></math>, VRAM budget for caching experts <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=V-U_{n}-U_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=V-U_{n}-U_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>), cache update frequency <math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, allocation granularity <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
              Set <math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> to 0  <span id="alg1.4.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;"> # the number of processed tokens</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
              Set <math id="alg1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> to 0  <span id="alg1.4.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;"># cache priority (<math id="alg1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[L],j\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">L</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[L],j\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>) </span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
              Set <math id="alg1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{i}(C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{i}(C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{i}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{i}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{PH}_{i}(a,C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏𝐇</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{PH}_{i}(a,C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> to 0  <span id="alg1.4.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;"># <math id="alg1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,C_{i}\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">C</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;" mathcolor="#9400D3" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,C_{i}\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
              Set <math id="alg1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{e}/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{e}/L</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to 0.5  <span id="alg1.4.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#9400D3;"># uniform allocation</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
              <span id="alg1.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> True <span id="alg1.4.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
              Process a token, and set <math id="alg1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\leftarrow q+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\leftarrow q+1</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
              Update <math id="alg1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{H}_{i}(C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{H}_{i}(C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}_{i}(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}_{i}(a)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{PH}_{i}(a,C_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏𝐇</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{PH}_{i}(a,C_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
              <span id="alg1.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> (<math id="alg1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\mod\tau==0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>mod</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\mod\tau==0</annotation></semantics></math>) <span id="alg1.4.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> (device is idle) <span id="alg1.4.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
              <math id="alg1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{V_{i}\}_{i\in[L]},\{\theta_{i}^{*}\}_{i\in[L]}\!\leftarrow\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{V_{i}\}_{i\in[L]},\{\theta_{i}^{*}\}_{i\in[L]}\!\leftarrow\!</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.4.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VramAllocation</span> (<math id="alg1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{e},\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{e},\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>) 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
              Update the expert cache for each layer 

</div>
<div id="alg1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
              <span id="alg1.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">Function<span id="alg1.4.12.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> VramAllocation (<math id="alg1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{e},\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ζ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{e},\zeta</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span>: 
</div>
<div id="alg1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
